# .ncp-consumer — declares how this repo pins NCP, for NCP's generic, consumer-
# agnostic pin tooling (check-consumer-pins.sh / repin-ncp.sh). NCP holds no
# knowledge of this repo; it discovers us by globbing for this file. Format:
# "<type> <relative-path> <release-label> <40-hex-revision>" per line; see
# NCP/INTEGRATING.md. The revision rows need NCP consumer tooling at commit
# 205384508d619923e05aef192bedaeb57cf665fc or later.
#
# CREBAIN pins the exact commit of the untagged NCP 1.0.0-rc.1 candidate (wire
# 1.0). The label is not a tag; the commit is the identity. NCP's grammar has no
# npm revision row, so scripts/check-ncp-coherence.sh checks that package.json
# and bun.lock pin the same commit.
cargo_rev       src-tauri/Cargo.toml                     v1.0.0-rc.1 2819dae3b6338bb1df6d105ebb5b7433936a993d
cargo_rev       src-tauri/crates/ncp-headless/Cargo.toml v1.0.0-rc.1 2819dae3b6338bb1df6d105ebb5b7433936a993d
cargo_lock_rev  src-tauri/Cargo.lock                     v1.0.0-rc.1 2819dae3b6338bb1df6d105ebb5b7433936a993d
